92186045417 true] [17592186434813 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434813 1077 "selection" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434813 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434802 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434813 1079 #uuid "f06a4c98-85ea-5abf-97e5-f6e83cf7c4d9" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434814 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434811 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434814 1069 "q-90542" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434814 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434814 1071 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈1.238\\,10,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{7}, & 1\\le x<2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434814 1072 #uuid "3460e358-579f-58c7-a5d7-39a789a5fd57" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434814 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{35}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ≈1.882\\,54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈1.882\\,54-(1.238\\,10)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434815 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434813 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434815 1069 "q-90563" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434815 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434815 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{8},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434815 1072 #uuid "6db9e5d7-25dc-58b4-9c16-44c0fcc1885a" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434815 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{x}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{24}|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{x}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{32}|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =8-{(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434816 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434812 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434816 1069 "q-90604" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434816 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434816 1071 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=0.65,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & 1\\le x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434816 1072 #uuid "c2971ed6-5542-5d1d-88ad-8eaa0189b83c" 13194139534744 17592186045417 true] [17592186434816 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{15}|}_{0}^{1}+{(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =0.6-(0.65)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139534744 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0318bf00-2d3f-5298-8b97-5d17613e6b6b" 17592186434796 "answer-37830293-bdeb-5123-98bd-4a580c5a69ae" 17592186434797 "answer-41f13a11-98cd-524c-94dd-97a4fbc4171f" 17592186434798 "answer-485c7842-588b-51d3-8fd7-892f4cb6ee0d" 17592186434799 "answer-522d10c3-4afd-53c7-b537-41d31c849e7f" 17592186434800 "answer